- * whole file, so an advance never has to refill it. Writing is not done:
- * opening for write fails, as with a read-only disk. */
+ * The backing file is loaded into guest memory; FOURCC_MEM borrows the
+ * caller's storage. SetBuffer creates an independent direct-I/O window at
+ * the current file position. It must start at the sought PCM payload, not
+ * at the file's RIFF header. Writing to disk is not implemented. */
